WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.651
Hi, I'm Sandra, from HEARa.

2
00:00:02.651 --> 00:00:06.549
Welcome to Day 2 of our 10 day Lip reading Challenge,

3
00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:11.151
designed to help you develop and practice your lip reading skills!

4
00:00:11.151 --> 00:00:14.531
Hearing loss can have a profound impact on your life.

5
00:00:14.531 --> 00:00:16.380
It touches every interaction.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.860
It can affect your career,
your relationships, 

7
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.042
and your happiness.

8
00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:28.840
Join me to explore tips and tricks on this YouTube channel
to bring confidence and clarity 

9
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.734
to relationships in all areas of your life.

10
00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:35.542
You probably guessed from the thumbnail

11
00:00:35.627 --> 00:00:39.300
that the answer to the question from day 1 is: Banjo.

12
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:49.020
The word banjo is very similar to mango.
Watch: banjo, mango. 

13
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.320
If we were talking about music,
you probably wouldn't confuse these two words. 

14
00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:02.400
That's why context is super important
when you're lip reading. 

15
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.400
Huge clues about context
come from the topic and the lingo  

16
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.673
and vocabulary associated with that topic.

17
00:01:11.673 --> 00:01:16.014
Context is also about where you are, who you're with, 

18
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.920
what you're doing,
and what you're about to do. 

19
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.700
And when you know the context, you can 
anticipate which words will follow.

20
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.381
Be aware of the clues around you

21
00:01:33.381 --> 00:01:36.840
and anticipate,
and you will become a speech reader!

22
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.180
Now you have the opportunity to 
experience this for yourself. 

23
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:48.780
We'll get some practice lip reading 
P, B, and M sounds in sentences. 

24
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.899
Keep in mind that the level 
of difficulty is critical. 

25
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.720
If it's too hard you won't learn as much 
and you won't enjoy learning, either. 

26
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.120
And I do want you to enjoy yourself.

27
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:13.140
In a lip reading class it's my job as the teacher 
to manage the level of difficulty for you, 

28
00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.980
but because this is YouTube 
and not an interactive class, 

29
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.120
it's your job to find that 
sweet spot of difficulty. 

30
00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.760
Please support your own learning and 
take the time to do that if you need to. 

31
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:32.460
I will show you how in a moment, but first let's 
see how you do with the first group of sentences. 

32
